  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CHOGM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The planning process for the Commonwealth Heads of Government Meeting (CHOGM) adopts a collaborative and phased approach, guided by ongoing consultations with key stakeholders and member states. During the current planning period, meetings are actively underway to map out activities, side events, and forums that will form part of the overall CHOGM programme. These discussions ensure that the agenda remains responsive to emerging priorities and aligns with the Commonwealth&#x2019;s strategic objectives. As planning progresses and details are confirmed, the programme will be continually refined and updated to reflect new developments, logistical considerations, and stakeholder input&#x2014;ensuring a well-coordinated and impactful event that delivers on the Commonwealth&#x2019;s shared goals. Outcomes and commitments agreed at CHOGM are implemented through targeted programmes, technical cooperation, and capacity-building initiatives coordinated by the Commonwealth Secretariat and its partners. This ensures that policy dialogue at the highest level translates into tangible, measurable progress that supports peace, prosperity, and sustainable development across the Commonwealth.</narrative>
  </description>
